			{
				"type": "Comment",
				"start": 0,
				"end": 624,
				"data": "\n\tA wide inline element whose content is a nested inline ELEMENT (not text), followed by a\n\tNON-TERMINAL text run — another inline element follows it. The tail boundary after such an\n\telement is a per-width fill decision measured from the closing tag's own column: it hugs the\n\tintact closing tag when the tail fits and breaks when it does not, converging the hugged,\n\tspaced and newline authorings onto one fixed point. Prettier instead groups the boundary WITH\n\tthe element, so once the element is multiline the tail always drops — it keeps the own-line\n\tform stable (output_prettier) and re-breaks the hugged one.\n"
			},
			{
				"type": "Text",
